1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,000
Mining electrification is a production decision as
well as an energy decision. A fleet

2
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:12,000
can have enough daily energy and still miss its
target because chargers, grid capacity

3
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:18,000
and shift timing do not line up.

4
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:23,500
This is the English reviewer view. The synthetic
case has four underground loaders, a

5
00:00:23,500 --> 00:00:29,000
twelve-hour shift and a seventeen-hundred-tonne
target. We include degraded batteries, charging
losses, critical site

6
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:34,500
load and a charger outage. These are declared
assumptions, not measurements from a real

7
00:00:34,500 --> 00:00:40,000
mine.

8
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:47,000
One charger delivers eleven hundred eighty-eight
tonnes. Two chargers on the same supply improve

9
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:54,000
output but still miss the target. Adding three
hundred fifty kilowatts reaches seventeen hundred

10
00:00:54,000 --> 00:01:01,000
eighty-two tonnes. Unmanaged charging reaches
similar output while overloading the supply.

11
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:08,333
Now inspect the upgrade and the next shift. Each
vehicle keeps its actual battery

12
00:01:08,333 --> 00:01:15,667
energy. A sixty-minute break restores the declared
initial charge in this case. The complete

13
00:01:15,667 --> 00:01:23,000
observation is twenty-five hours, so we do not
present it as a daily-production improvement.

14
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:30,000
The second workflow asks what evidence is missing.
Choose the technology, project stage and

15
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:37,000
jurisdiction. Battery swapping needs a pack-stock
review. Trolley needs a route and line review.

16
00:01:37,000 --> 00:01:44,000
Declaring a document available changes the dossier,
but never certifies a permit.

17
00:01:44,000 --> 00:01:51,000
Here is a real NVIDIA Nemotron request through
Nebius Token Factory. Inspect the executed

18
00:01:51,000 --> 00:01:58,000
tools. The model retrieves the dossier and sources,
then selects evidence identifiers. The application

19
00:01:58,000 --> 00:02:05,000
validates that selection and fills the report with
catalog text and computed counts. The

20
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:12,000
provider key stays on the server.

21
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:17,333
Reports can be exported for inspection. The code,
tests and integration records make results

22
00:02:17,333 --> 00:02:22,667
reproducible. The operation is synthetic, and the
prototype does not control equipment, validate
industrial

23
00:02:22,667 --> 00:02:28,000
savings or replace electrical and safety
engineering.

24
00:02:28,000 --> 00:02:34,000
ElectroDecision helps planners compare charging
choices and organize the next engineering review.
The next

25
00:02:34,000 --> 00:02:40,000
step is validation with site data and users. Thank
you.
